.\" sliverctl(1). Source of truth for commands: crates/sliverctl/src/cli.rs (a test keeps this
.\" page in sync with `sliverctl help`). Prose: docs/api.md, docs/customization.md.
.TH SLIVERCTL 1 2026-10-12 "sliver 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sliverctl \- control the Touch Bar and publish items to it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sliverctl
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B sliverctl publish
.RI [ options ]
.IR type : id [: label ]...
.br
.B sliverctl config
.I subcommand
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B sliverctl preset
.BR export | show | import
.I file
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sliverctl
talks to
.BR sliver\-agent (1)
over the session D\-Bus API
.RI ( io.github.wawow830.Sliver ),
the same API every app and script can use.
It can inspect the bar, drive it the way
.B pkill \-RTMIN+N waybar
drives waybar, and publish buttons that stay on the bar for as long as
.B sliverctl publish
runs.
.PP
The
.B config
and
.B preset
commands work offline: they edit the configuration file
(see
.BR sliver\-config (5))
and never touch D\-Bus.
The agent picks the change up by itself.
.PP
.I MODULE
is any module id:
a built\-in
.RB ( clock ,
.BR battery#bat2 ),
a user module
.RB ( custom/vpn ),
or an item published by an app
.RB ( app/org.example.App#item ).
.SH INSPECTING
.TP
.B status
Agent health, active layer and profile, display state (on, dimmed, off), and the API version.
.TP
.B modules
Every module with its id, type, source, visibility and placement.
.TP
.B contexts
Contexts published by apps and scripts: provider, scope, and whether they are on screen.
.SH CONTROLLING
.TP
.B reload
Reload the configuration.
Errors are printed, and the exit status is 1 if there are any.
An invalid configuration is never applied.
.TP
.BI validate " file"
Check a configuration file without applying it.
.TP
.BI signal " n"
Re\-run every module configured with
.BI "signal = " n\fR.
.B RTMIN+\fIn\fR
is accepted too.
.TP
.BI refresh " module"
Re\-run one module now.
.TP
.BI show " module\fR, " hide " module\fR, " toggle " module"
Change a module's visibility until the agent restarts.
The configuration file isn't touched.
.TP
.B reset\-visibility
Undo every
.BR show ,
.B hide
and
.BR toggle .
.TP
.BI tap " module\fR, " hold " module\fR, " double\-tap " module"
Fire the module's binding for that gesture, as if it had been touched.
.TP
.BI trigger " module gesture"
The same for any gesture:
.BR tap ,
.BR hold ,
.BR double\-tap ,
.BR swipe\-left ,
.BR swipe\-right ,
.BR drag .
.TP
.BI update " module key" = "value ..."
Push output to a custom module that has no
.BR exec ,
using the keys a script would print:
.BR text ,
.BR icon ,
.BR class ,
.BR percentage ,
.BR alt ,
.BR tooltip .
.TP
.BI "layer switch" " name"
Make
.I name
the current layer.
.TP
.BI "layer push" " name \fR[\fPtimeout-ms\fR]"
Open a layer on top, optionally closing it again after
.IR timeout\-ms .
.TP
.B layer pop
Close the top layer.
.TP
.BI "layer toggle" " name"
Open the layer, or close it if it is open.
.TP
.BI layout " name"
Force a layout until the context changes.
.TP
.BI profile " name"
Switch to another profile (see
.BR sliver\-config (5)).
The agent refuses a profile that doesn't validate and keeps the current one.
.TP
.BR bar " " show | hide | toggle
Blank or restore the whole bar.
The safe hatch (press Fn twice and hold) still works while the bar is hidden.
.TP
.BI "var set" " name value"
Set a user variable, usable in rule conditions.
.TP
.BR render " [" \-\-layout
.IR file ]
.BR \-o | \-\-output
.I out.png
Render a layout with the agent's renderer and save it as PNG.
.SH PUBLISHING
.B sliverctl publish
creates a context, puts the given items on the bar, and keeps running.
It prints one line per event,
.IP
.IR "item kind " [ key = value ...]
.PP
for example
.B "go tap"
or
.BR "vol value value=0.4 phase=change" .
The items disappear when
.B sliverctl
exits.
If
.B sliver\-agent
restarts, they are published again automatically.
.PP
Items are written
.IR type : id [: label ]
with
.I type
one of
.BR button ,
.BR toggle ,
.BR label ,
.BR slider ,
.BR progress ,
.BR spacer ,
.BR segmented .
.TP
.BR \-\-scope " " app | status | target
Where the items show.
.B status
(the default) puts them in the user's Status items.
.B app
shows them while one of this process's windows is focused.
.B target
shows them while another app is focused (see
.BR \-\-target\-app ).
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " id"
Stable reverse\-DNS id.
The user's settings for these items (hide, reorder, pin, style) are keyed by it, and so are module ids
.RB ( app/\fIid\fP#\fIitem\fP ).
.TP
.BI \-\-title " text"
Name shown in the settings app.
.TP
.BI \-\-target\-app " app-id"
For
.BR "\-\-scope target" .
.TP
.B \-\-modal
Cover the Main and Controls zones while shown, if the user allows it.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR \fIid.key\fB=\fIvalue\fR, \fB\-\-prop\fR \fIid.key\fB=\fIvalue\fR
Set any item property
.RI ( docs/api.md
\(sc3), for example
.BR "\-p go.icon=media\-playback\-start" .
This option can be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-stdin
Read
.IR "id key" = "value ..."
lines from standard input and apply them as updates.
Quote values that contain spaces:
.BR "go label='Going now'" .
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B sliverctl config
edits the user configuration file.
Comments are kept, and an edit that would make the configuration invalid is refused.
.TP
.B config path
Where sliver looks for its configuration.
The file in use is marked with
.BR * .
.TP
.BR "config check " [ \fIfile\fP ]
Parse and validate.
The exit status is 1 if there are errors.
.TP
.BI "config get" " key"
For example
.B modules.clock.format
or
.BR rules[0].layout .
.TP
.BI "config set" " key value"
.I value
is TOML
.RB ( 8 ,
.BR true ,
.BR """x""" ,
.BR "{ key = ""F1"" }" )
or a bare string.
.TP
.BI "config unset" " key"
Remove a key.
.TP
.BR "config resolve " [ \fIlayer\fP "] [" \fIctx\fP = \fIvalue\fP ...]
Show which layout and modules would be on the bar in a given context, for example
.BR "app_id=foot locked=true" .
.TP
.BR "config import\-tiny\-dfr " [ \-\-force ]
Write
.B config.toml
and
.B style.css
from tiny\-dfr's configuration.
.TP
.BR "config import\-waybar " [ \fIfile\fP "] [" \-\-force ]
Write
.B config.toml
from a waybar configuration.
.TP
.BR "config profile " [ list ]
List profiles; the active one is marked with
.BR * .
.B default
is
.BR config.toml .
.TP
.BI "config profile use" " name"
Make
.I name
the active profile without asking the agent; a running agent follows.
.TP
.BR "config profile new " \fIname\fP " [" \-\-from " \fIprofile\fP]"
Create a profile: your main configuration plus its own changes, or a copy of
.IR profile .
.TP
.BI "config profile rename" " old new"
.TQ
.BI "config profile rm" " name"
Rename or delete a profile.
Deleting the active one switches to
.BR default .
.SH PRESETS
A preset is one
.B .sliver
file holding a whole setup: the configuration, its includes, the stylesheet with its imports, and
the icons and images the configuration points at.
It is a TOML document
.RB ( [preset] " and " [files] ;
binary files are base64), so you can read it before using it.
.TP
.BR "preset export" " \fIfile\fP [" \-\-name " \fIname\fP] [" \-\-config " \fIpath\fP]"
Bundle the configuration in use (or
.IR path ).
Files outside the configuration directory are copied into
.B assets/
or
.BR include/ ,
and the references to them are rewritten.
System files under
.BR /usr ,
.B /etc
and
.B /opt
are referenced, not copied.
.B env
tables are left out, since that's where secrets live.
Commands that mention your home directory are pointed out.
A configuration with errors is refused.
.I file
gets the
.B .sliver
extension if it has none;
.B \-
writes to standard output.
.TP
.BI "preset show" " file"
List the files and everything the preset would run as you:
module scripts
.RB ( exec ,
.BR exec\-if ),
and the commands, D\-Bus calls, files and URLs opened by its gestures and menus.
Then check that it loads.
The exit status is 1 if it doesn't.
.TP
.BR "preset import" " \fIfile\fP [" \-\-yes "] [" \-\-no\-commands "] [" \-\-dir " \fIdir\fP]"
Replace your configuration with the preset.
It shows what
.B preset show
shows and asks first:
answer
.B yes
to import it as it is, or
.B no\-commands
to import it with every script and command removed.
.B \-\-yes
and
.B \-\-no\-commands
answer in advance; without a terminal, one of them is required.
A preset whose configuration doesn't load is refused and nothing changes.
Files it replaces are copied to
.BI backups/ time /
in the configuration directory first, and
.B config.toml
is written last, so the agent reloads a complete setup.
.B \-\-dir
installs somewhere other than
.BR ~/.config/sliver .
.SH VALUES
In
.IR key = value
arguments,
.B true
and
.B false
are booleans, integers are 32\-bit integers, decimals are doubles, and anything else is a string.
Prefix a value with
.B s:
to force a string
.RB ( text=s:42 ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the agent reports an error or isn't running (or a preset doesn't load or an
import is cancelled), and 2 for usage errors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The session bus to use.
.SH EXAMPLES
A button that runs a build:
.PP
.EX
sliverctl publish \-\-provider org.example.Build button:build:Build |
  while read \-r item kind _; do
    [ "$kind" = tap ] && make \-C ~/src/project
  done
.EE
.PP
A label updated by a script:
.PP
.EX
while sleep 2; do echo "load label='$(cut \-d' ' \-f1 /proc/loadavg)'"; done |
  sliverctl publish \-\-provider org.example.Load \-\-stdin label:load:load
.EE
.PP
waybar\-style control:
.PP
.EX
sliverctl signal 8
sliverctl update custom/status text='deploy ok' class=ok
sliverctl layer push media 5000
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sliver\-agent (1),
.BR sliver\-config (5),
.BR sliver\-stylesheet (5),
.BR sliverd (8),
.BR busctl (1)
.PP
.I docs/api.md
and
.I docs/user\-guide.md
in the sliver sources.
